@PACKAGE_INIT@

# Imprint — the install-tree consumption entry (Batch G P1.5).
# The exported targets mirror the add_subdirectory consumption names
# (ARCHITECTURE §3.2): imprint::imutil/imcore/imevent/iminput/imui/
# imapp/imapp_canvas/snapshot, the shell targets built by the
# generating configuration (imprint::shell_common/shell_hostloop/
# shell_backend, platform-dependent), and the C ABI (imprint::zbapi +
# its installed header) when the generating build had the binding (X-1).

# X-2: the shell targets' platform link requirements resolve through
# imported targets, so the consumer has to be able to find them before
# imprintTargets.cmake names them. Deliberately a *soft* find: the
# dependency belongs to the shell targets, not to the package, so a
# headless consumer of a shell-carrying package configures without
# libx11-dev (the X-3 rule, install side) — a consumer that does link a
# shell target without X11 gets a generate-time error naming X11::X11.
# The generating configuration bakes the line in (empty for backends
# whose requirements are plain linker flags, e.g. FB / SIXEL / AppKit).
@IMPRINT_SHELL_FIND_DEPENDENCY@

include("${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/imprintTargets.cmake")

check_required_components(imprint)
